From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 18:16:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] main: handle execvp failure on restart

netifd_restart() brings all interfaces down before re-executing
itself. When the exec failed (e.g. binary replaced mid-upgrade or a
relative argv[0]), the callback simply returned, leaving the daemon
alive with every interface down, no log message and no retry. Log the
failure and exit so procd respawns the daemon.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
(cherry picked from commit 1595cd7b25da95b80b5e500d1a7546fc4350e92c)
---
 main.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/main.c b/main.c
index 6655e00..f114b4a 100644
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 #include <signal.h>
 #include <stdarg.h>
 #include <syslog.h>
+#include <errno.h>
 
 #include "netifd.h"
 #include "ubus.h"
@@ -271,6 +272,10 @@ netifd_kill_process(struct netifd_process *proc)
 static void netifd_do_restart(struct uloop_timeout *timeout)
 {
 	execvp(global_argv[0], global_argv);
+
+	/* all interfaces are already down; exit so procd can respawn us */
+	netifd_log_message(L_CRIT, "Failed to restart netifd: %s\n", strerror(errno));
+	exit(1);
 }
 
 int netifd_reload(void)
